*! cleanplots14vr v1.1.0 Trenton Mize 2026-10-12
*! Reversed ordinal companion scheme to cleanplots: 14 sequential viridis colors
*
* Same 14 palette colors as cleanplots14v, in exactly reverse order.
* Low categories are darkest; high categories are lightest (dark purple to light yellow).
* Retains the cleanplots legend, sizing, symbols, and line patterns.
*
* Color source: viridis (van der Walt & Smith 2015); sampled at end=.95, reversed.
* Matching R scale:
*   scale_color_viridis_d(option = "viridis", end = 0.95, direction = 1)
*   Note: matching endpoints require begin=.0; direction=1 produces a
*   dark-to-light scale, from darkest to end=.95 (rather than 1.0).
*   Use begin=0, end=.95 explicitly when comparing.
*
* Colors recycle after 14 plots; Stata has 15 plot slots.
* Bar and area color settings inherit the 70 percent intensity.
* Example: graph bar price, over(rep78) asyvars scheme(cleanplots14vr)

#include cleanplots


color p1              "68 1 84"
color p1line          "68 1 84"
color p1lineplot      "68 1 84"
color p1markline      "68 1 84"
color p1bar           "68 1 84"
color p1barline       "68 1 84"
color p1area          "68 1 84"
color p1arealine      "68 1 84"
color p1pie           "68 1 84"
linepattern p1line solid
linepattern p1lineplot solid
symbol p1 smcircle

